an8.30:23.1 starts: “Having understood my thoughts,
an8.30:23.2 starts: the unsurpassed teacher in the world
an8.30:23.3 starts: came to me by psychic potency
an8.30:23.4 starts: in a mind-made body.
an8.37:4.1 starts: Having thus practiced charity
an8.37:4.2 starts: with a mind freely generous,
an8.37:4.3 starts: one intelligent and wise, rich in faith,
an8.37:4.4 starts: is reborn in a pleasant, unafflicted world.
an8.38:4.3 starts: Firm in faith, the pious man,
an8.38:4.4 starts: having known their good qualities,
an8.38:5.1 starts: venerates the homeless renouncers,
an8.38:5.2 starts: the mendicants who lead the spiritual life.
an8.46:19.1 starts: She does not despise her husband,
an8.46:19.2 starts: the man who constantly supports her,
an8.46:19.3 starts: who ardently and eagerly
an8.46:19.4 starts: always brings her whatever she wants.
an8.46:20.1 starts: Nor does a good woman scold her husband
an8.46:20.2 starts: with speech caused by jealousy;
an8.46:20.3 starts: the wise woman shows veneration
an8.46:20.4 starts: to all those whom her husband reveres.
